### Users — /users
#
# "Register a reader" stores the new reader's id, which loans.http then uses.

### Register a reader — 201.
# The address is lower-cased before it is stored and compared, so registering the same address in
# different casing afterwards is a 409 rather than a second reader — a duplicate would split one
# person's loan history in two. Running this twice therefore answers 409 — correctly; change the
# address to seed another reader.
POST {{host}}/users
X-Actor: {{actor}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Silva",
  "email": "ana.silva@example.com"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.id) {
        client.global.set("userId", response.body.data.id);
        client.log("Stored userId " + response.body.data.id);
    }
%}

### Read a reader's loans — 200, or 404 when no reader holds that identifier.
# 404 rather than an empty page, which would be indistinguishable from a reader who has never
# borrowed anything.
#
# This is the reader's history, not their current shelf: returned and cancelled loans are included.
GET {{host}}/users/{{userId}}/loans?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20
X-Actor: {{actor}}

### Read only what a reader is currently holding — 200.
GET {{host}}/users/{{userId}}/loans?status=Active
X-Actor: {{actor}}
